Z||000000||mindscape||07-16-2001||09:45 PM||||What am I doing..,  Rebuilding an 1988 2.8 as a 3.1 and have a fuel injector question.  I cannot afford new injectors or service at the moment.  However, a fellow I know owns a junk yard.  He has offered a set from a 1988 Corsica 2.8 and a similar set from a Camaro of unknown year but most likely an 1988/1989; suppose to be a 1991 but has a 2.8 a plenum.<P>I assume old stale watery gas is a bad sign.  I know the aftermarket injectors for the Fiero/Camaro are the same for 1988 and 1989.<P>If I'm correct the two sets are disc type whereas the Fiero uses a pintle?<P>What is a good way to test?<P>What ia a good way to clean?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||07-17-2001||01:43 AM||||Can't help, but I'm looking for a little injector info.<P>So....*BUMP*<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000002||mindscape||07-17-2001||11:01 PM||||I have two sets of injectors to choose from.  However, both are Multec.  What I've read about them is not encouraging; short life span - internal coil shorting - something about injector clearner stripping away the magnet wire insulation.  The other issue with the Multec versus the stock Pintle type is resistance.  The stock injectors have a little over 16 ohms of resistance, whereas the Multec have around 12 ohms.  I don't want to fry my new ECM.  Physically the Multec injectors from a 1988/1989 Corsica/Beretta 2.8 or 1990/1991 Camaro 3.1 will work.  If I'm not mistaken the Multec injectors is actually more efficient, but suffers from an atypical short life span.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||West Coast Fiero||07-17-2001||11:06 PM||||we offer injector cleaning here at West Coast Fiero, we can clean and inspect all of you injectors for $12 a piece. They will fire like new when returned.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000004||mindscape||07-17-2001||11:42 PM||||Considering that the plastic end of one of the injectors is broken up around the O-ring I'm placing my bets on finding a set up at Corley's salvage yard.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Much better price. Of course they have to work...  What do you think about using a set of Multec's from a 1990/1991 Camaro?||||reg||1
Z||000005||West Coast Fiero||07-18-2001||01:02 AM||||New 2.8 injectors from GM are nearly $210 a peice, bear that in mind when deciding to go with new ones||||reg||1
